## 5. Official / player-side context

- **Blizzard "Defense Matrix" (Season 12, Aug 2024)** — official news (overwatch.blizzard.com):
  - **500,000+ accounts banned** for cheating; **40,000+ accounts** suspended/banned for grouping
    with cheaters.
  - **Console peripheral detection** (Season 11): unapproved mouse/keyboard peripherals used in
    console pools cause loss of Competitive access and relegation to the PC input pool for unranked
    modes.
  - **Avoid-as-Teammate list**: up to 15 players, 3 of which can be pinned; non-pinned entries
    decay after 7 days.
  - **In-match reporting**: scoreboard controls to mute any player's text/voice chat and file a
    two-click report.
  - **Streamer Protect restriction**: the "Hide My Name" feature is now limited to players who
    completed the **Unrelenting Hero** challenge (1,750 wins), to stop cheaters/disruptors hiding
    behind fresh low-time accounts.
  - Blizzard states they are "hard at work on new anti-cheat technologies" but **withholds
    implementation details**.
- **Blizzard forums (2020–2021)** — sustained community discussion on why Blizzard has **not**
  adopted a kernel driver (Vanguard/Ricochet-style). Privacy, security, and Linux/Mac player
  access are the cited reasons. Overwatch's AC remains **user-mode only**.
- **UC wiki** — Overwatch pairs Warden with **GuardIT** (Arxan) to prevent debugging (historical
  note; current analysis centers on the Warden/Eidolon split).
- **Related community tooling**: `[Release] Eidolon Anti-Anti-Debug` (thread 776838) and the
  decryption/Xor release (715241) show an active bypass ecosystem around these layers.

